---
title: Banana bread
servings: 12
yield: 1 loaf
tags: [american, vegetarian, make-ahead]
cuisine: american
time: 1 hour 30 minutes
source: Banana Bread by King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/banana-bread-recipe
---

Heat the oven to 325°F (165°C). Lightly grease a #9x5-inch loaf pan{}.

Beat the @unsalted butter{8%tbsp}(cool room temperature),
@brown sugar{2/3%cup}(packed, light or dark), @vanilla extract{1%tsp},
@ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp}, @baking soda{1%tsp},
@baking powder{1%tsp} and @table salt{1%tsp} in a #large bowl{} until smooth.

Beat in the @bananas{1.5%cup}(mashed),
@jam{3%tbsp}(apricot, or orange marmalade; optional), @honey{1/4%cup} and
@eggs{2}.

Add the @all-purpose flour{2.25%cup} and @walnuts{1/2%cup}(chopped, optional)
and mix just until smooth.

Spread in the pan and leave ~{10%minutes} at room temperature.

Bake ~{45%minutes}, then lay foil loosely over the top and bake ~{25%minutes}
more, until a toothpick comes out with a few moist crumbs. Give it another 5
minutes if not.

Cool ~{10%minutes} in the pan, then turn out and cool completely on a rack.
